Skills: SDD Ecosystem

Purpose:
  SDDRA ecosystem-specific skills for integration, event processing,
  field mapping, notification dispatch, and scheduled sync. These skills
  are derived from production codebases under ./tmp/ and encode the
  concrete patterns used across sweeps-integrations, pultapaz, and
  rovio-matchmaking.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
    1  @INDEX.sdd
    2  @SKILL-INTEGRATION-MODULE.sdd
    3  @SKILL-EVENT-PROCESSOR.sdd
    4  @SKILL-FIELD-MAPPING.sdd
    5  @SKILL-NOTIFICATION.sdd
    6  @SKILL-SCHEDULED-SYNC.sdd

Modes:
  LEARN    — learn SDD ecosystem patterns
  APPLY    — apply patterns to new integrations
  REVIEW   — review implementation against skills
  UPGRADE  — propose skill improvements

Rules:
  [S1] Integration modules MUST have explicit boundaries.
  [S2] Event processors MUST implement claim/handle/complete lifecycle.
  [S3] Field mapping MUST be config-driven, not hardcoded.
  [S4] Notifications MUST support multi-channel dispatch with daily limits.
  [S5] Scheduled sync MUST be idempotent and observable.

Entry:
  Read:
    INDEX.sdd
    SKILL-INTEGRATION-MODULE.sdd

  Resolve:
    integration-module
    event-processor
    field-mapping
    notification
    scheduled-sync

Navigation:
  IntegrationModule: @SKILL-INTEGRATION-MODULE.sdd
  EventProcessor: @SKILL-EVENT-PROCESSOR.sdd
  FieldMapping: @SKILL-FIELD-MAPPING.sdd
  Notification: @SKILL-NOTIFICATION.sdd
  ScheduledSync: @SKILL-SCHEDULED-SYNC.sdd

State: +
